<BaseLayout title="About">
    <div class="container page-intro">
        <h1>About</h1>
            <p>Well, here we are. A page that seems so essential, it feels daunting to tackle. So for now, we won't. Instead, all you need to know now is the following: </p>
            <p>I'm here to try new things, confront new curiosities, challenge my consciousness. I'd like to build a small home for myself and find that my mirror holds a collective consciousness. My mirror holds memory.</p>
            <p>It sounds silly, and yet here we are.</p>
            <p>I'm here to explore myself through the lens of learning web development and design. Nothing is stable or promised here, except for the mountain of courage it takes to muster up and go public with something like this.</p>
            <p>As a girlie with a chronic condition and a neurospicy mind, no topic is really off limits. I spend time, daily, shaping my biology to fit my current reality; for once, I am creating a space that'll shift to accommodate my biology. There is no space for shame here, from myself or anyone else. Whoever lands here, cosmically agrees to leave shame at the door.</p>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
